      Through the doorway at the back there is a second room: metal shelving stacked with boxes, two red lockers, a sink with a mirror over it, buckets and cleaning supplies on the floor, and a black-and-white tiled floor with a maze pattern cut into one corner of it. The stockroom is where the second half of the level happens, and it is also where the level stops being about numbers. The two red lockers are the thing to remember — one of them carries the five-symbol lock that the pencil and paper are for.
